IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nii-il34-nouns`

-- National Insurance Law s 2 (פריסת תשלומים חריגים, spreading exceptional payments) and Schedule A (לוח א׳). Row IL-34, priority 5.
-- `src:N` is line N of the Law's deposited text (../../registers/source-bundle/national-insurance-law-consolidated-version-5755-1995.he.wiki.txt,
-- sha256 78bf47ee...2a97).
--
-- WHAT IT SAYS. In computing the average wage for benefits and contributions, the measured wage (the CBS's average wage per employee post) of an
-- "exceptional wage month" (the last month of a tax year, and a month in which clothing or recuperation allowances were paid to most employees) is
-- replaced by the "corrected measured wage"; and the average wage so computed is raised by one-twelfth of the sum of the "monthly differences" of the
-- last three exceptional months (s 2(b)). Schedule A fixes the minimum average monthly income of a self-employed person (s 1 "עובד עצמאי"): 15% of the
-- average wage as it is on the 1st of the first month of each quarter, for each month of the quarter.
--
-- WHAT IS NOT HERE. The measured wages themselves are the Central Bureau of Statistics's, and are inputs; so is the average wage on the day Schedule A names.
-- Row IL-04 encodes s 1 "the average wage" (the three-month average and the compensation rate) and takes Schedule A's sum as an argument; this module
-- computes that sum. The consolidation's note gives 13,769 for the measured wage in 2026 (s 2(a)) and 13,566 for the average wage (s 1); neither is used in
-- a rule, only in tests as the Institute's printed 2026 figure.

§ `Section 2 and Schedule A`

§§ `Section 2(a): the definitions`

