-- src:231 | (א) בסעיף זה –
-- src:232 | ”שכר מדוד“ – שכר ממוצע למשרת שכיר שמפרסמת הלשכה המרכזית לסטטיסטיקה;
-- src:233 | [note: נכון לשנת 2026, השכר הממוצע המדוד הוא 13,769 ש״ח.]
-- src:234 | ”חודש שכר חריג“ – החודש האחרון של שנת מס וכן חודש שבו שולמו תוספות בעד ביגוד או בעד הבראה למרבית העובדים השכירים;
-- src:235 | ”שכר מדוד מתוקן“ – השכר המדוד של החודש האחרון שקדם לחודש שכר חריג (להלן – החודש הקודם), בתוספת 0.5% ממנו ובתוספת פיצוי שחל בחודש השכר החריג; היה החודש הקודם חודש שכר חריג, יובא בחשבון, לענין זה, במקום השכר המדוד של החודש הקודם, השכר המדוד של החודש האחרון שקדם לחודש הקודם בתוספת 0.5% ממנו ובתוספת פיצוי שחל בחודש הקודם.
-- src:236 | (ב) בחישוב השכר הממוצע, לצורך גמלאות ודמי ביטוח, יחולו שינויים אלה:
-- src:237 | (1) לגבי חודש שכר חריג, במקום השכר המדוד יובא בחשבון השכר המדוד המתוקן;

-- "Exceptional wage month": the last month of a tax year (December), or a month in which clothing or recuperation allowances were paid to most
-- employed persons. The second limb is a fact the caller reports.
@ref National Insurance Law s 2(a), "חודש שכר חריג" (source line 234)
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `clothing or recuperation allowances were paid to most employees in the month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(a) — month` `the month` `is an exceptional wage month, allowances to most employees being` `clothing or recuperation allowances were paid to most employees in the month` MEANS
    IF `the month` LESS THAN 1 OR `the month` GREATER THAN 12
    THEN REFUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"
    ELSE `the month` EQUALS 12 OR `clothing or recuperation allowances were paid to most employees in the month`

@ref NOTES.md fork W1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 2(a) adds "compensation" and does not say whether as a rate of the earlier month's measured wage or as an amount in shekels` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 2(a) adds \"compensation\" and does not say whether as a rate of the earlier month's measured wage or as an amount in shekels"

-- The addition for compensation, to a base measured wage, at a reading. Nothing is added when no compensation applied (rate 0 and amount 0): the
-- readings agree, and none is consulted.
@ref National Insurance Law s 2(a), "שכר מדוד מתוקן" (source line 235); NOTES.md fork W1
GIVEN c    IS A `The compensation that applied in a month`
      base IS A NUMBER
      r    IS A `A reading of the compensation added in section 2(a)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the addition for compensation` c `to the measured wage` base `, reading it as` r MEANS
    IF c's `its rate` EQUALS 0 AND c's `its amount in shekels` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE
        CONSIDER r
        WHEN `the compensation is added as its rate of the earlier month's measured wage` THEN base TIMES (c's `its rate`)
        WHEN `the compensation is added as its amount in shekels`                         THEN c's `its amount in shekels`
        WHEN `how the compensation is added is declined`                                  THEN `section 2(a) adds "compensation" and does not say whether as a rate of the earlier month's measured wage or as an amount in shekels`

-- "Corrected measured wage": the measured wage of the last month before the exceptional wage month, plus 0.5% of it, plus the compensation that
-- applied in the exceptional month; and if that last month was itself an exceptional wage month, the measured wage of the last month before IT, plus
-- 0.5% of it, plus the compensation that applied in IT.
@ref National Insurance Law s 2(a), "שכר מדוד מתוקן" (source line 235); NOTES.md fork W1
GIVEN `the measured wage of the last month before the exceptional month` IS A NUMBER
      `that last month was itself an exceptional wage month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measured wage of the last month before that one` IS A NUMBER
      `the compensation in the exceptional month` IS A `The compensation that applied in a month`
      `the compensation in the earlier exceptional month` IS A `The compensation that applied in a month`
      r IS A `A reading of the compensation added in section 2(a)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(a) — the corrected measured wage: the month before measured` `the measured wage of the last month before the exceptional month` `, that month being exceptional:` `that last month was itself an exceptional wage month` `, the month before it measured` `the measured wage of the last month before that one` `, compensation then` `the compensation in the exceptional month` `and in the earlier exceptional month` `the compensation in the earlier exceptional month` `, reading it as` r MEANS
    IF `that last month was itself an exceptional wage month`
    THEN `the measured wage of the last month before that one` TIMES 1.005
         PLUS `the addition for compensation` `the compensation in the earlier exceptional month` `to the measured wage` `the measured wage of the last month before that one` `, reading it as` r
    ELSE `the measured wage of the last month before the exceptional month` TIMES 1.005
         PLUS `the addition for compensation` `the compensation in the exceptional month` `to the measured wage` `the measured wage of the last month before the exceptional month` `, reading it as` r

@ref NOTES.md fork W1 (SHRUG, Meng 2026-10-08)
GIVETH A `A reading of the compensation added in section 2(a)`
`s 2(a) — the reading this row takes of the compensation added` MEANS `how the compensation is added is declined`

@ref National Insurance Law s 2(a), "שכר מדוד מתוקן" (source line 235)
GIVEN `the measured wage of the last month before the exceptional month` IS A NUMBER
      `that last month was itself an exceptional wage month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measured wage of the last month before that one` IS A NUMBER
      `the compensation in the exceptional month` IS A `The compensation that applied in a month`
      `the compensation in the earlier exceptional month` IS A `The compensation that applied in a month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(a) — the corrected measured wage: the month before measured` `the measured wage of the last month before the exceptional month` `, that month being exceptional:` `that last month was itself an exceptional wage month` `, the month before it measured` `the measured wage of the last month before that one` `, compensation then` `the compensation in the exceptional month` `and in the earlier exceptional month` `the compensation in the earlier exceptional month` MEANS
    `s 2(a) — the corrected measured wage: the month before measured` `the measured wage of the last month before the exceptional month` `, that month being exceptional:` `that last month was itself an exceptional wage month` `, the month before it measured` `the measured wage of the last month before that one` `, compensation then` `the compensation in the exceptional month` `and in the earlier exceptional month` `the compensation in the earlier exceptional month` `, reading it as` (`s 2(a) — the reading this row takes of the compensation added`)

§§ `Section 2(b): the average wage for benefits and contributions`

-- src:238 | (2) השכר הממוצע יחושב בכפוף להוראות פסקה (1) ויוגדל בשיעור השווה לחלק השנים עשר של סך ההפרשים החודשיים לגבי שלושת חודשי השכר החריג האחרונים, ששכרם המדוד ידוע ביום העדכון; לענין זה, ”הפרש חודשי“ – ההפרש שבין השכר המדוד של חודש שכר חריג לבין השכר המדוד המתוקן של אותו חודש, מחולק בשכר המדוד המתוקן של החודש האמור;
-- src:239 | (3) [note: (פקעה).]

-- "Monthly difference": the difference between the measured wage of an exceptional month and its corrected measured wage, divided by the corrected one.
@ref National Insurance Law s 2(b)(2), "הפרש חודשי" (source line 238)
GIVEN `the measured wage of the exceptional month` IS A NUMBER
      `its corrected measured wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(b)(2) — the monthly difference: measured` `the measured wage of the exceptional month` `and corrected` `its corrected measured wage` MEANS
    IF `its corrected measured wage` EQUALS 0
    THEN REFUSE "a monthly difference is divided by the corrected measured wage, which is 0"
    ELSE (`the measured wage of the exceptional month` MINUS `its corrected measured wage`) DIVIDED BY `its corrected measured wage`

@ref National Insurance Law s 2(b)(2) (source line 238)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 2(b)(2) takes the last three exceptional wage months, and more than three monthly differences were given` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 2(b)(2) takes the last three exceptional wage months, and more than three monthly differences were given"

-- (b)(1): for an exceptional wage month the corrected measured wage is used in place of the measured wage (the caller computes the average wage
-- from those). (b)(2): the average wage so computed is increased by a rate equal to one-twelfth of the sum of the monthly differences of the last
-- three exceptional wage months whose measured wage is known on the update day. The caller gives those differences, at most three.
@ref National Insurance Law s 2(b)(2) (source line 238)
GIVEN `the average wage computed subject to (1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the monthly differences of the last exceptional wage months known on the update day` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(b)(2) — the average wage increased: computed` `the average wage computed subject to (1)` `with the monthly differences` `the monthly differences of the last exceptional wage months known on the update day` MEANS
    IF count `the monthly differences of the last exceptional wage months known on the update day` GREATER THAN 3
    THEN `section 2(b)(2) takes the last three exceptional wage months, and more than three monthly differences were given`
    ELSE `the average wage computed subject to (1)` TIMES (1 PLUS (sum `the monthly differences of the last exceptional wage months known on the update day`) DIVIDED BY 12)

§§ `Schedule A: the minimum average monthly income of a self-employed person`

-- src:4360 | ⟦ח:קטע2|לוח א|לוח א׳|אחר=[לוח א׳]⟧
-- src:4361 | ⟦ח:קטע4||[note: (סעיף 1, הגדרת ”עובד עצמאי“)]⟧
-- src:4362 | ⟦ח:קטע4||הכנסה מזערית חודשית ממוצעת לעובד עצמאי⟧
-- src:4365 | לגבי כל אחד מהחודשים שברבעון – סכום השווה ל־15% מהשכר הממוצע, כפי שהוא ב־1 בחודש שבתחילת כל רבעון; לענין זה, ”רבעון“ – תקופה רצופה של שלושה חודשים שתחילתה ב־1 בינואר, ב־1 באפריל, ב־1 ביולי או ב־1 באוקטובר של כל שנת מס.

-- "For each of the months of the quarter, a sum equal to 15% of the average wage as it is on the 1st of the month at the start of each quarter."
-- The average wage on that day is an input (it changes on 1 January and on the first day of a month with a compensation).
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule A (source line 4365)
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the average wage on the first day of the quarter's first month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Schedule A — the minimum average monthly income for month` `the month` `, the average wage on the first day of the quarter's first month being` `the average wage on the first day of the quarter's first month` MEANS
    IF `the month` LESS THAN 1 OR `the month` GREATER THAN 12
    THEN REFUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"
    ELSE 15% TIMES `the average wage on the first day of the quarter's first month`
